<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Frederick Francis IV, Grand Duke of Mecklenburg-Schwerin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1882–1945</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Friedrich Franz IV of Mecklenburg-Schwerin</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Frederick Francis IV was the last Grand Duke of Mecklenburg-Schwerin, reigning from 1897 to 1918, and from February 1918 also regent of Mecklenburg-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/strelitz">Strelitz</a>. His state kept one of the most old-fashioned constitutions in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, dominated by the noble estates. He abdicated on 14 November 1918, and Mecklenburg-Schwerin became a free state with a parliamentary constitution.</p></div>
